{% extends "base.html.jinja2" %}
{% import "components.html.jinja2" as macros %}
{% block title %}How to play - Cross Kings{% endblock %}

{# A board diagram in the compact mobile-card style, with the marker on
   `marker`, gold outlines on every cell in `legal`, blue outlines on every
   cell in `pick`, and `taken` cells drawn as gaps. With `dim` set, every
   cell that isn't the marker or highlighted is greyed out. #}
{% macro diagram(board, marker, legal, taken, caption, pick=none, dim=false) %}
<figure class="htp-diagram">
    <div class="diagram-board">
        {% for row in board %}
            {% set r = loop.index0 %}
            {% for card in row %}
                {% set c = loop.index0 %}
                {% set cell = (r, c) %}
                {% set highlighted = (cell in legal) or (pick and cell in pick) or (marker and cell == marker) %}
                <div class="diagram-cell{% if cell in legal %} legal{% endif %}{% if pick and cell in pick %} pick{% endif %}{% if dim and not highlighted %} dim{% endif %}">
                    {% if cell in taken %}
                        {{ macros.draw_card(None, marker=(cell == marker)) }}
                    {% else %}
                        {{ macros.draw_card(card, marker=(cell == marker)) }}
                    {% endif %}
                </div>
            {% endfor %}
        {% endfor %}
    </div>
    <figcaption>{{ caption }}</figcaption>
</figure>
{% endmacro %}

{# A single row of cards for the scoring examples. #}
{% macro cardrow(cards, caption) %}
<figure class="htp-diagram">
    <div class="diagram-hand">
        {% for card in cards %}{{ macros.draw_card(card) }}{% endfor %}
    </div>
    <figcaption>{{ caption }}</figcaption>
</figure>
{% endmacro %}

{% block content %}
<div class="how-to-play">
<h1>How to play Cross Kings</h1>

<p>Cross Kings is a two player card game. It uses a small deck &mdash; Ace
through 8 in every suit, plus the four Kings, 36 cards in all. Over the
course of a game you each collect cards from a grid, and at the end you
score the cards in your hand for runs and sets. The player with more
points wins.</p>

<h2>The board</h2>

<p>The 36 cards are dealt into a 6&times;6 grid. The cards on the two
diagonals are dealt <strong>face down</strong>; every other card is face
up.</p>

{{ diagram(board, none, [], [],
   "The deal: the two diagonals are dealt face down (green); every other
    card is face up.") }}

<p>A single marker &mdash; a blue dot &mdash; sits on the grid and
shows the current position. It starts on one of the four central cards. 
The player who is <em>not</em> moving first chooses which of the four 
central face-down cards to start the marker on at the start of the game</p>

{{ diagram(board, none, [], [],
   "The four central face-down cards: whoever isn't moving first picks
    which one the marker starts on.", pick=central_cells, dim=true) }}

<h2>Making a move</h2>

<p>When the marker has been placed, the game starts and players take 
alternating turns. On your turn you move the marker to any card in the 
<strong>same row or column</strong> as its current cell, and collect that 
card into your hand. You must move the marker on the very first turn 
&mdash; you can't take the card the marker starts on</p>

<div class="htp-legend">
    <span><span class="swatch htp-swatch-marker"></span>marker (current position)</span>
    <span><span class="swatch htp-swatch-legal"></span>a card you could move to</span>
</div>

{{ diagram(board, move_marker, move_legal, [],
   "Every gold-outlined card is a legal move from the marker: the whole
    of its row and its column.", dim=true) }}

<h2>Gaps, and the end of the game</h2>

<p>Taking a card leaves a gap in the grid. The marker can slide straight
<strong>over any gaps</strong> left by cards already taken, so it can
still reach a card further along the same row or column.</p>

{{ diagram(gap_board, gap_marker, gap_legal, gap_taken,
   "Later in the game: the marker sits in a gap and reaches cards beyond
    the other empty gaps in its row and column.", dim=true) }}

<p>The game ends when the marker is left with no card remaining in its row
or column &mdash; there is nowhere left to move. Both players then score
the cards they have collected.</p>

<p>Both hands are open the whole game: you can always see which cards your
opponent has taken. When a face-down card is collected, it is revealed to
both players.</p>

<h2>Scoring</h2>

<p>At the end, each player scores the cards they collected. You earn
points for two kinds of group:</p>

<div class="htp-columns">
    <div>
        <p><strong>Runs</strong> &mdash; consecutive cards of the same suit.</p>
        {{ cardrow(run_cards, "A run of three clubs, 4-5-6.") }}
    </div>
    <div>
        <p><strong>Sets</strong> &mdash; cards that share the same rank.</p>
        {{ cardrow(set_cards, "A set of three 7s.") }}
    </div>
</div>

<p>A single card can count towards a run <em>and</em> a set at the same
time. A group needs at least three cards to score: three cards are worth 3
points, and every additional card beyond that adds another 2 points.</p>

<details class="htp-details">
    <summary>Show scoring table</summary>
    <div class="table-scroll">
    <table class="score-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Run or set length</th><th>Points</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            {% for length, points in points_table %}
            <tr><td>{{ length }}</td><td>{{ points }}</td></tr>
            {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
    </table>
    </div>
</details>

<h2>Kings are wild</h2>

<p>A King can stand in for any card to help complete a run or a set,
whichever scores you the most. There is a catch: each King that forms
part of a scoring group makes that group worth <strong>one point
less</strong> than it otherwise would be.</p>

<p>Any Kings you collect will be automatically placed in the highest
scoring positions for you as you play</p>

{{ cardrow(king_cards,
   "5-6 of hearts with a King filling in for the 7: a run of three worth
    3 - 1 = 2 points.") }}

<p>Your total score is the sum of every run and set you can form from your
hand. The higher total wins; equal totals are a draw.</p>

<h2>Ready to play?</h2>

<p>
    <a href="{{ url_for('play') }}"><button type="button">Play vs computer</button></a>
    <a href="{{ url_for('index') }}"><button type="button">Create or join a room</button></a>
</p>
</div>
{% endblock %}
